item.description:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;Wired&lt;/i&gt; has the &lt;a href="https://www.wired.com/story/hacked-prayer-app-sends-surrender-messages-to-iranians-amid-israeli-strikes/?_sp=cac71a7f-c88a-42bc-b4ca-23c1ce88f702.1772641675776"&gt;story&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;Shortly after the first set of explosions, Iranians received bursts of notifications on their phones. They came not from the government advising caution, but from an apparently hacked prayer-timing app called BadeSaba Calendar that has been downloaded more than 5 million times from the Google Play Store.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The messages arrived in quick succession over a period of 30 minutes, starting with the phrase &amp;#8216;Help has arrived&amp;#8217; at 9:52 am Tehran time, shortly after the first set of explosions. No party has claimed responsibility for the hacks...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
